{"title":"How plants make their own food using sunlight","key_idea":"Plants use sunlight, water, and air together to make glucose food and release oxygen.","method":["Identify the three raw materials plants need: sunlight from the sun, water from the soil through roots, and carbon dioxide from the air through leaf pores.","Understand that the plant uses sunlight as energy to combine these materials.","Remember that the plant produces two things: glucose (food to help it grow) and oxygen (which we breathe)."],"worked_example":{"problem":"A plant on a sunny windowsill has soil with water and air around it. What does it need to make food?","steps":["The plant gets sunlight through the window.","The plant gets water from the wet soil through its roots.","The plant gets carbon dioxide from the air through tiny pores in its leaves.","The plant uses all three together to make glucose and oxygen."],"answer":"The plant needs sunlight, water from soil, and carbon dioxide from air to make its own food."},"key_terms":[{"term":"photosynthesis","meaning":"the process plants use to make food using sunlight"},{"term":"glucose","meaning":"the sugar food that plants make and use to grow"},{"term":"carbon dioxide","meaning":"a gas in the air that plants take in through their leaves"}],"common_mistakes":["Thinking plants get all their food from the soil—in fact, soil gives only water, and the plant makes its own food using sunlight.","Forgetting that plants need air as well as water and sunlight."],"remember":"Sunlight plus water plus air equals plant food and oxygen.","quick_check":[{"q":"Name the three things a plant needs to make food.","a":"Sunlight, water from soil, and carbon dioxide from air."},{"q":"What two things does a plant produce when it makes food?","a":"Glucose (food) and oxygen."}],"tell_your_child":"Think of your plant like a little cook in the kitchen: it gathers ingredients from the sun, ground, and air, then mixes them together to make its own meal. That's how plants feed themselves and make the air fresher for us too."}
```
